  "notes": "{補|ほ} means 'to supplement' or 'to replenish,' and {水|すい} means 'water.' {補水|ほすい} is commonly used in health and fitness contexts, especially during summer when heatstroke prevention is a major public health concern in Japan.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {補水|ほすい}する (to rehydrate)\n- {補水|ほすい}{液|えき} (rehydration solution, oral rehydration fluid)\n- {経口|けいこう}{補水|ほすい}{液|えき} (oral rehydration solution — ORS)\n- こまめに{補水|ほすい}する (to rehydrate frequently)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {水分|すいぶん}{補給|ほきゅう} — hydration, fluid intake (more common in everyday speech; same meaning but longer)\n- {給水|きゅうすい} — water supply (providing water to a system or area, not specifically about drinking)",
